{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA — mechanism proven (rebar-debug Phase 1)\n\n**Root cause (single, changeable artifact):** `src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py`,\nthe not-pinned arm of `classify_plan_review_attestation` (the `keyring is None` branch, ~L238-246).\nThe classifier resolves the DSSE principal from the attestation envelope, calls\n`trusted_env.trusted_env_keyring(principal, repo_root)`, and returns an affirmative\n`{\"verdict\": \"mismatch\"}` whenever that principal is absent from `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`.\n`mismatch` is in `FLAG_VERDICTS`, so `bucket_for_verdict` returns `flag` and\n`apply_bugfix_size_gate` sets `verdict[\"verdict\"] = \"BLOCK\"`. The rejection is on the SOURCE of\ncertification (who signed), never on whether a plan review actually happened.\n\n**Discriminating runtime proof:** `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py::test_classify_unpinned_foreign_environment_flags`\nexecutes the classifier against a real fixture store holding a genuinely minted, genuinely signed,\nsame-material plan-review op-cert whose env is simply not pinned. It observes `verdict == \"mismatch\"`\nand `bucket == \"flag\"`. Its sibling `test_classify_pinned_foreign_environment_reaches_accepted`\nholds every other variable constant and differs ONLY in whether `trusted_environments.yaml` pins\nthe env — and reaches `certified`/`accepted`. The pair discriminates provenance from plan quality:\nidentical review, identical material, opposite verdicts. Both pass on `main` today, so the arm is\nlive, not theoretical.\n\n**Legitimacy:** `defect` / `incomplete-implementation` against this ticket's own AC1 and AC3 (the\nauthoritative statement of intended behaviour), which the 75cdfec357 pin left unmet.\n\n## Fix plan (operator's design decision — implemented as current policy, not a config framework)\n\nThe attestation check must NOT gate on the SOURCE of certification. It gates ONLY on the FACT that\nan attested plan review has been completed, plus that attestation's lifecycle/freshness validity.\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` — delete the cross-host source-of-certification\n   chain: the `trusted_env_keyring` lookup + not-pinned `mismatch` arm, the `verify_opcert` call,\n   and `_plan_review_anchor` (whose only consumer was `verify_opcert`'s era anchoring). The chain\n   becomes: attestation record present -> decodable op-cert envelope -> `compute_validity`\n   lifecycle/freshness. The verdict vocabulary shrinks to the `compute_validity` literals plus the\n   gate's own `error`; unknown literals still fail OPEN (infra/advisory).\n2. `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` — RED oracle: invert\n   `test_classify_unpinned_foreign_environment_flags` into\n   `test_classify_unpinned_foreign_environment_is_accepted`, and realign the vocabulary tests.\n3. `docs/plan-review-gate.md` — new section documenting the Gerrit bugfix-size attestation gate\n   and its executable remedy (AC1).\n4. `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` — the author-facing on-ramp for the same (AC1).\n5. AC3 is satisfied by removal: the message that named no remedy is gone, and the only remaining\n   blocking finding is the teaching finding, which names `rebar review-plan <id>`.\n\nExplicitly out of scope, and deliberately so: no op-cert service client, no configurable\ntrust-policy framework. This is the current policy, \"for now\"."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785891863878427001,"uuid":"470990c0-7aa0-4d38-87ac-8884d2d32c6a"}